The web process on a system without EGL (WPE port, ThreadOS)

WebKit's web process makes an EGL display before its first page,
and ends itself when it cannot: a system without a GPU is expected
to have Mesa's software EGL. ThreadOS has no EGL library at all, and
the first EGL call through libepoxy would abort on not finding one.
WebKit can paint without one - Skia on the processor, into shared
memory (NonCompositedFrameRenderer, the SharedMemory swap chain) -
and every path that would want the display asks
ProcessCapabilities::canUseAcceleratedBuffers() first. So when
libepoxy finds no EGL (epoxy_has_egl() asks without aborting), the
web process says buffers cannot be accelerated and makes no display.

--- a/Source/WebKit/WebProcess/glib/WebProcessGLib.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebKit/WebProcess/glib/WebProcessGLib.cpp
@@ -39,6 +39,7 @@
 #include <WebCore/ProcessCapabilities.h>
 #include <WebCore/ScreenProperties.h>
 #include <WebCore/SystemSoundManager.h>
+#include <epoxy/egl.h>
 
 #if ENABLE(REMOTE_INSPECTOR)
 #include <JavaScriptCore/RemoteInspector.h>
@@ -149,6 +150,15 @@
     if (PlatformDisplay::sharedDisplayIfExists())
         return;
 
+    // A system with no EGL library at all draws pages on the processor:
+    // there is no display to make, and every path that would want one
+    // asks canUseAcceleratedBuffers() first. (epoxy_has_egl() asks
+    // without aborting, as the first EGL call through epoxy would.)
+    if (!epoxy_has_egl()) {
+        ProcessCapabilities::setCanUseAcceleratedBuffers(false);
+        return;
+    }
+
 #if USE(GBM)
     if (m_rendererBufferTransportMode.contains(RendererBufferTransportMode::Hardware)) {
         bool disabled = false;
